      "body": "Worth putting in the description? Validating cannot pick the arm either, because a block with no spends comes back byte identical at verbosity 2 and 3, since a coinbase input has no `prevout` to add, and arm 3 lists `prevout` without requiring it, so both arms accept both responses and the `oneOf` does not resolve. That answers the reviewer who asks why a consumer cannot just validate, which the current wording leaves open. Already true on the base.",
